[A10] Owner decision on the round 7 STOP (issuecomment-6353806286), and the round 7b assignment for [A659] on PR #770. The head is 5282b8b6 (not pushed).

**Owner decision (2026-10-23 06:32, option (a), "keep a for now").** This PR's slice growth on route-1x1 is accepted beyond the +80 slice tolerance: +107 slices against #771's record, leaving 15 of 15,850 slices on the shipping image.
- This extends the block-RAM exception (#632 issuecomment-6309313685) to the measured LUT/FF/slice deltas of this PR: +500 LUT, +376 FF, +107 slices and +2 RAMB18.
- Mark II (#640) recovers the area. Until then, the next growth on the shipping image has no slice room and needs its own owner decision.

Round 7b, on 5282b8b6 with new commits, no rebase and no amend:
1. **Re-record the resource gate.** Re-record the three endpoints (route-1x1, ooc-1x1, ooc-8x8) with the recipe at the head, citing both exceptions: the block-RAM one above and this comment. Record the per-shape figures. `pp_resource_gate.py check` must exit 0 against the new record.
2. **Finish item 4 of the round 7 assignment** (issuecomment-6351804497) at the head:
   - the full sweep;
   - Yosys;
   - the firmware gate set;
   - the docs gates under make 4.3, if any file changed;
   - lint;
   - the builder bank;
   - all three full campaigns: TDM8 render 31, pull-in 18 + history, GM-step 22. The merge changed their inputs.
3. **Update the PR body and HANDOFF.** Add a Round 7 section with the exception citation, the re-recorded figures and the gate table.

STOP if any gate or campaign fails, or if the re-recorded route differs from the round 7 measurement in LUT, FF or slices.
